<title>USA: Consumers investigates Palisades shutdown.</title>
<headline>Consumers investigates Palisades shutdown.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumers Power Co said it was investigating the cause of a shutdown at its 780 megawatt Palisades nuclear power plant and had not yet set a date for the plant to resume electricity production.</p>
<p>The plant was shut Thursday after a problem with electrical equipment at a main generator, company spokesman Mark Savage said Friday.</p>
<p>Consumers will investigate the problem over the weekend, and may have a restart estimate by Monday, Savage said.</p>
<p>The Palisades plant is located in South Haven, Mich. and makes up about 18 percent of Consumers power generation capacity, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>Consumers Power is a subsidiary of CMS Energy Corp.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627))</p>
